                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "19916415",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198013237122",
                            "num_reviews": 19,
                            "playtime_forever": 237,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 87,
                            "last_played": 1504453144
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I like difficult games, and puzzle platformers.\nThis game had high potential but the implementation is very poor.\nAt first I saw the game had jumpack action and a sort of grappling hook and I went WOW this is gonna be great.\nA game that relies on precise timming, jumping, triggering switches should have been awesome.\nAnd here is where everything goes wrong.\nWhen activating the jumpjets the screen trembles, which means your aim will be randomly thown in any direction. I mean if the game relies on aiming and jumping to test the player skill then said player should be allowed to aim as good as he can right? The aim problem is further compounded by the autoaim of the grapple. Yes, you read it right. In a game that tests aiming skill you have autoaim (besides the random aim described earlier)...\nThen there is the platforming: jumpjets and being able to airwalk should make platforming a pleasure. But no! The walls have almost no texture which makes it very difficult to get an idea of the direction you go in mid air. You see the same color metalilc wall and is difficult to say in which way the character goes. It is thus very difficult to execute the precision jumping required by the game.\nIf the developers read the reviews:\n- please eliminate the screen tremble when activating jump jets\n- eliminate (or give an option to eliminate) the autoaim of grapple\n- offer much more visual clues to indicate the mid air speed of the player (simplest way to do this is to texture the walls and place some doodads in the rooms)",
